  <name>Gitilante</name>
  <summary>Review Git changes and manipulate single hunks</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Gitilante is a lightweight Git GUI focused on the operations that are
      more convenient graphically than in a terminal: reviewing the current
      changes and staging, unstaging, discarding or reverting single hunks,
      with a fast view of the history.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is a thin frontend over the git executable and deliberately does not
      replace the command line: commits, branches, merges and everything else
      stay in your terminal workflow.
    </p>
  </description>
